# p_7e4a — Evening Kitchen (Revised): Board Stays, Knife Goes Home, Dishes to Cupboard (fork of p_8c3d)

Fork of p_8c3d. The parent's "Act Three: wash at sink" narrative for the cutting board and kitchen knife is contradicted by the evidence. The cutting board is seen at counter_k1 on all three sighted days (3/3) and the kitchen knife is seen at drawer_k_k1 on all three sighted days (3/3). After cooking, the board simply stays on the counter (or is set aside there) and the knife is put back in its drawer. Only the pan, pot, and the snack bowl actually go to the sink for rinsing. Additionally, the snack bowl is at cupboard_k1 at 18:00 on day 1 (before dinner), not at the sink — its "usual place" of sink_k1 (2/3 of days) reflects the washing-up moment, not the resting state. Priya's bowl and glass also go to cupboard_k1 after dinner rather than lingering at the sink.

What changed: (1) cutting_board post-cooking location is counter_k1, not sink_k1; (2) kitchen_knife post-cooking location is drawer_k_k1, not sink_k1; (3) snack_bowl has a daytime block at cupboard_k1; (4) added blocks for bowl_priya and glass_priya going to cupboard_k1 after dinner. The three-act structure is preserved but Act Three is narrower: only pan, pot, and snack bowl go to the sink.

